This project adapts work from the following sources. Per-skill provenance, including
the specific files adapted and the commit or fetch date they were taken at, is recorded
in each skill's skill-source.json.

emilkowalski/skills — MIT License
https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills
Copyright (c) Emil Kowalski

    The workflow archetypes this collection is built on — construct, adversarial review,
    read-only audit producing plans for a cheaper executor — and a substantial part of its
    motion craft. Adapted as principles and re-grounded in Android behaviour rather than
    copied; see the Provenance section of STANDARDS.md for which rules derive from it and
    what each one changes.

pbakaus/impeccable — Apache License 2.0
https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
Copyright (c) Paul Bakaus

    The anti-anchoring review structure used by review-android-motion: an unanchored
    design assessment and a deterministic findings assessment, produced in isolation, with
    the findings withheld from synthesis until the assessment returns. The rules, guidance
    and detectors are not adapted from it.

